Load a saved preset from its own file path

setupPresets() reads the preset files of the configuration directories.
It computes the absolute path of each file, and then keeps the bare file
name. The preset map therefore holds a name that resolves against the
working directory of the process.

Every reader of the map needs a path. setPreset() gives the name of the
preset to qtcReadConfig() and to KConfig. These calls do not find the
file, so the dialog applies the default settings. The colour pickers
then show black, and the check boxes show the default flags. A save
after that load writes the default settings over the settings file of
the user.

The delete button tests the name against the home directory of the user.
The test fails for a bare name, so the button stays off for a preset
that the dialog found at the start. savePreset() stores the full path,
so the map holds two kinds of name.

This change keeps the absolute path that the search computes. The map
then holds one kind of name. The load reads the file of the preset from
any working directory. The export and import paths keep their behaviour.

The delete button now works for a preset of the home directory. A preset
outside that directory stays a system preset, because the home directory
test still fails for it.

The Qt 5 dialog holds the same code and takes the same change.

The change sits on the branch work/preset-path of the local tree. The fork
wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !12 on system/qtcurve holds that
branch as the source.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt5/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt5/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 68d11854..518abb6d 100644
--- a/qt5/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt5/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -1722,7 +1722,7 @@ QtCurveConfig::setupPresets(const Options &currentStyle,
     // TODO custom filter and figure out what directory to use.
     QStringList files;
     {
-        // Make unique list of relative paths
+        // Make a unique list of absolute paths
         QHash<QString, QString> files_map;
         QStringList dirs = QStandardPaths::locateAll(QStandardPaths::GenericConfigLocation,
                                                      QStringLiteral("QtCurve"),
@@ -1734,7 +1734,7 @@ QtCurveConfig::setupPresets(const Options &currentStyle,
                 if (!files_map.contains(file)) {
                     auto abspath = d.absoluteFilePath(file);
                     files_map.insert(file, abspath);
-                    files.append(file);
+                    files.append(abspath);
                 }
             }
         }
